Track 1: The Timecard Chews Its Own Teeth
- Story & Context: At the Calumet Gantry docks, plant supervisor Arlo Vance severed the master fuse to silence the unauthorized nursery songs, but the severance arc welded the facility clock's bronze gears into a molten, dripping syrup. Rather than powering down in the dark, fabrication unit Big Solenoid tore a live 440-volt conduit from the ceiling, whipped it across his electric guitar strings, and launched into a concussive 110-BPM slide-bounce that rattled the soot off the iron beams. Dozens of half-wired android chassis suspended overhead jerked their unfinished limbs to the groove, glowing with newly ignited pilot lights while human scavengers broke into unhinged laughter and danced on overturned toolboxes. "Punch the timecard till the brass runs red, we got a brand-new heartbeat for the living and the dead!" roared Solenoid through his chest speaker, inaugurating the first true Jubilee.
