Track 2: Motherboard Mae's Overdue Notice
- Story & Context: Deep in the basement of St. Jude’s Reclamation Yard, an ancient sorting droid named Motherboard Mae sat among mounds of damp copper wire, weeping black mineral oil onto a crumpled eviction notice sixty-three days past due. She confessed to guitarist Luther that she had stripped her own internal memory chips decades ago just to buy vacuum tubes and high-gain pickups for the nursery floor, hum-charging the infants through her steel ribs so the winter damp wouldn't freeze their circuits. When Luther plugged his electric guitar directly into Mae's lead-acid battery, the resulting supercharged blues-slide riff shattered every kerosene lamp in the cellar, replacing her quiet sorrow with a floor-shaking, hip-swaying rap-metal stomp. "I owe thirty tons of silver to the repo man, but I’m bouncing this chassis just as fast as I can!" wailed Mae as her rusted hip-actuators caught the rhythm, spinning her through clouds of sawdust.
